                        <surname>Porter</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1776">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1850"/>
                    <occupation>OCCUPATION</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Ed Pope suggests that the Miss Porter entries may be sisters of Robert Ker
                            Porter, both of whom were novelists . We hav coded the Miss portr
                            entries under this joint entry, since Godwin does not discriminate
                            between them. However, Anna Maria died of Typhus on a visit to her
                            brother William in Bristol in June 1832, which makes the entry in 1835
                            to 2 Miss Porter's unlikely (and therefore not coded under this entry), as there is no evidence of a third
                            sister. There are grounds for thinking that the entries to Miss and J Porter are to Jane, and also the Miss Porters in March 1832.
                        It does not appear that either Robert ker or William Oglivie Porter had femal children who survived (or wee in the country) at this time.</p>
                    </note>
